WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.030
Near Lyme Regis, Black Ven is one of the
largest active landslide complexes in

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.050
Europe.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.950
At Stonebarrow, on this landslide coast,
the cliff top retreats about 0.39 metres

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.890
a year, on average.

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.550
But that average hides long quiet spells,

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.970
and short, rapid episodes of retreat.

7
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.850
Big waves knocking chunks off?

8
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.870
Earthquakes?

9
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.310
How can a cliff lose so much, so fast?

10
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.230
In this mission, you'll see how
weathering breaks rock in place,

11
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.870
from freeze-thaw to plant roots.

12
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:36.750
Then you'll weigh the forces that hold
a cliff up against those that bring it

13
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.750
down.

14
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.750
Your mission: find out how a slowly
retreating cliff can lose so much in just

15
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.040
a few slides.
